  "title": "Knowing About Biases Doesn’t Automatically Protect You",
  "description": "Knowing about biases doesn’t automatically protect you. Here’s how to act: - Practice self-awareness: Regularly check if biases might be influencing you. - Get external input: Ask others for feedback to catch blind spots. - Use checklists: Create simple steps to avoid falling into known biases. Example: Knowing about confirmation bias doesn’t stop you from doing it. Actively seek opposing views instead.",
